@meta (title: "Open a local document", locale: "en-US")

# Open a local document

Choose your platform to see the relevant file-opening instructions. This guide
assumes you already have a local HTML document exported from tinta.

@choice platform = "macOS" (
  options: ["macOS", "Windows", "Linux"],
  label: "Your platform",
)

@when platform == "macOS"
In Finder, locate the HTML file and open it with your browser.
@end

@when platform == "Windows"
In File Explorer, locate the HTML file and open it with your browser.
@end

@when platform == "Linux"
In your file manager, locate the HTML file and open it with your browser.
@end

## Keep an editable copy

An HTML export is for reading. Keep the original `.tinta` source for later edits.

@details "If the document includes images"
A `.tinta.zip` source bundle keeps the source and its local images together.
An HTML export already embeds the images it needs.
@end
